 "goals": {
  "0": "The password is right in the page source.",
  "1": "Right-click is blocked by JavaScript \u2014 but only in a browser.",
  "2": "The page loads an image from a browsable /files/ directory.",
  "3": "Even Google won't find this one \u2014 but robots.txt talks.",
  "4": "Access is granted only to visitors referred from the natas5 site.",
  "5": "Login state lives in a cookie you control.",
  "6": "The source code reveals a secret stored in an include file.",
  "7": "An include parameter is used without any validation.",
  "8": "The secret is 'encoded' in the source: bin2hex(strrev(base64(x))). Encoding is not encryption.",
  "9": "A search form feeds your input straight into a grep command.",
  "10": "Same form, but ; | & are filtered now. Spaces and grep's file arguments are not.",
  "11": "The 'data' cookie is base64 of a repeating-key XOR of known JSON \u2014 recover the key and forge an admin cookie.",
  "12": "An upload form keeps your file's .php extension.",
  "13": "The upload now checks the file type with exif_imagetype \u2014 so make the PHP look like a GIF.",
  "14": "A login form builds its SQL query with your username inside it.",
  "15": "The form only says whether a user exists \u2014 a blind SQL injection oracle. Brute-force the password through it.",
  "16": "The dictionary search filters shell metacharacters but not $() command substitution \u2014 turn it into a yes/no oracle and extract the password character by character."
